**24**, Craig **19**, Roland **7**, Claire **9**, Bob **34**.</p><p>- CRM caveat stated: reporting is only accurate “where it’s been added correctly” (source tagging/data entry inconsistency).</p><p>#### Vs Last Week / Last Month</p><p>- No prior referral snapshot provided.</p><p>#### What’s Working Well</p><p>- Strong referral base relative to peers when captured correctly.</p><p>#### What’s Not Working Well</p><p>- Inconsistent referral/source logging undermines MI and attribution.</p><p>- Behavioural gap: referral asks not yet embedded consistently at the key moments.</p><p>#### Risks / Blockers</p><p>- Under-reporting and misattribution of lead sources; reduced visibility of what is driving performance.</p><p>- Missed easy-win opportunities if referral asks are not systematic.</p><p>#### Actions Required</p><p>- Ask for referrals systematically at:</p><p>  - **Mortgage offer issued**</p><p>  - **Mortgage completion**</p><p>- Ensure referral/source is logged correctly in CRM; request clients copy Karen into an intro email or provide a contact number.</p><p>#### Action Owner</p><p>- **Adviser:** Karen Lochhead</p><p>#### Trend Insight</p><p>- **Stagnant:** referral volumes are healthy, but improvement is constrained by inconsistent referral asks and inconsistent CRM source logging.</p><p>---</p><p>## Overall Performance Diagnosis</p><p>#### Adviser Strengths This Review</p><p>- Strong effectiveness when engaged: **61% conversion** on contactable/spoken-to clients.</p><p>- Protection performance above average: **45% penetration** vs team **43.9%**, with higher premium/case size.</p><p>- Strong income position: **~£35,000 projected**, and **94% banked rate** (**137/145**).</p><p>#### Main Risks</p><p>- **Lead follow-up inconsistency** and aged CRM stages (including **07/10/2025**) driving leakage and unreliable reporting.</p><p>- **Report completion delays** are the primary bottleneck slowing admin handover, protection progression, and quarter-end banking.</p><p>- Protection pipeline drift on named cases (**Michael Cooper**, **Lucy Muir**, **Byron Stevens**, **Alexandria P**) if not chased/closed promptly.</p><p>#### Behaviour Patterns / Accountability Concerns</p><p>- Karen acknowledged reduced outbound lead chasing.</p><p>- Repeated pattern of delaying reports after advice despite prior intentions.</p><p>- Ownership gaps risk where workflows exist but are not clearly reflected in CRM (owner/next action/date).</p><p>#### Where Management Support Is Required</p><p>- Enforce non-negotiable standards:</p><p>  - appointment outcome logging,</p><p>  - product status correctness (especially no-show/not proceeding),</p><p>  - same-day reports.</p><p>- Protect adviser/admin catch-up time to prevent repeated handover delays and late-day urgent requests.</p><p>---</p><p>## Master Action List</p><p>| Action | Client / Area | Owner | Deadline | Risk if not done |</p><p>| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |</p><p>| Validate and update outcomes for **7 “Appointment Booked”** leads (attended/no-show/DIP/lost) and correct statuses | Leads (last month: 28 total) | Karen + Megan | Not specified | Missed conversions; inaccurate MI; leads go cold |</p><p>| Audit **32** leads under **Created + Appointment Booked** (incl. items referenced back to **07/10/2025**): confirm last contact, owner, next step; decide **reactivate vs close** | Lead backlog | Karen + Megan | Not specified | Long-term leakage; inflated pipeline; ownership gaps |</p><p>| Review **13 DIP** clients: confirm last spoken to and next step; progress to application or move to nurture/close | DIP pipeline | Karen + Megan | Not specified | DIP cases stall; lost business without visibility |</p><p>| Review **11 Appointment Completed / Keeping in Contact** leads (incl. older Aug/Sep items referenced) to confirm still active and correctly worked | Nurture pipeline | Karen + Megan | Not specified | Time wasted on dead leads; missed reactivation opportunities |</p><p>| Progress to interview and 