00** (expected across March 2026 and April 2026).</p><p>- Banked rate: **137 banked / 145 written** = **~94%**.</p><p>## What is working</p><p>- Strong conversion when clients are engaged (**61%** on spoken-to clients).</p><p>- Protection performance is ahead of team average (**45%** penetration).</p><p>- Strong banking efficiency (**94%** banked rate).</p><p>## Identified risks</p><p>- Aged/stale lead statuses (including items referenced back to **07/10/2025**) and unclear appointment outcomes distort MI and create revenue leakage.</p><p>- Main bottleneck remains **reports not being completed immediately after advice**, delaying admin handover and increasing slippage risk.</p><p>- Protection cases may drop without timely follow-up and correct closure/status updates.</p><p>## Cases Requiring Attention</p><p>- **Billy Townsend:** needs interviewed; bad credit; clear next steps required. *(Owner: Karen)*</p><p>- **Byron Stevens:** no response (client in Iraq) — re-contact needed. *(Owner: Megan)*</p><p>- **Michael Cooper:** £164/month quote; GP report access from Vitality required; decide next step/transfer to Rita if no further movement. *(Owner: Karen / Rita; deadline 2026-03-31)*</p><p>- **Lucy Muir:** follow-up needed after Karen’s email; confirm proceed/decline and close/update. *(Owner: Megan)*</p><p>- **Alexandria P:** re-contact to confirm income/employment and appetite to proceed. *(Owner: Megan)*</p><p>- **Rachel McKinnon:** confirm “has cover” and close/update status if complete. *(Owner: Karen)*</p><p>## Revenue and Pipeline Risks</p><p>- Slippage risk if protection starts too late in **April 2026** (noted as “50/50” for banking before **2026-04-30**).</p><p>- Incorrect product status coding prevents correct platform nurture journeys and undermines re-engagement.</p><p>## Focus for Next Week</p><p>- Tighten lead handling discipline: confirm appointment outcomes, eliminate stale statuses, and re-engage or close aged leads.</p><p>- Remove CRM bottlenecks: **